
;; ============================================================
;; SoftwareBug subclass taxonomy : alpha / beta1 / beta2 / gamma
;; Sources : CWE-440, CWE-1059, CWE-758, CWE-703, ISO/IEC 9899:2018,
;;           IEEE 29148-2018, NIST SP 800-30 Rev.1, IEC 61882, SAE ARP4761A
;; ============================================================

(subclass Specification Proposition)
(termFormat EnglishLanguage Specification "specification")
(documentation Specification EnglishLanguage "A &%Proposition declaring how a
&%ComputerProgram, system, or component should behave, what properties it
should possess, or what constraints it should satisfy.  Mirrors the &%Policy
pattern : the &%Specification is the propositional content ; the act of
issuing it is a &%Declaring event whose &%agent is the specifying party.
Adapted from ISO/IEC/IEEE 24765:2017 3.3793 : 'document that specifies, in a
complete, precise, verifiable manner, the requirements, design, behavior, or
other characteristics of a system or component.'  A &%Specification may be
recorded in any &%ContentBearingObject via &%containsInformation.")

(=>
  (instance ?SPEC Specification)
  (exists (?AGENT ?DECL)
    (and
      (instance ?DECL Declaring)
      (agent ?DECL ?AGENT)
      (patient ?DECL ?SPEC))))

